    "narrative": "The anchor of our lineup today is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who at a 73.85 score represents our most reliable engine against Ure\u00f1a. While the raw base projection was solid, the +10% boost from the SP skill profile and the premium spot in the three-hole create an elite floor. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) and **Lawrence Butler** (69.79) are must-starts; **Aranda** benefits from a massive 12% platoon edge against Jobe, while **Lawrence Butler** is poised to exploit the hitter-friendly conditions in his matchup against Bradley, T, carrying a potent 13% platoon adjustment. **Jung Hoo Lee** also warrants attention; despite a slightly lower raw base, the combination of a favorable wind and an 11% boost from the SP matchup elevates his profile to a 64.35, making him a high-upside play for today\u2019s 5x5 categories.\n\nThe closest call on the bench was **Gleyber Torres**, who posted a 50.38 score\u2014just narrowly missing the cut behind the more efficient production profiles of **Yainer Diaz** and **Cal Raleigh**. While **Gleyber Torres** enjoyed a strong +10% boost from his lead-off spot, a significant -13% platoon penalty when facing Legumina ultimately forced him to the bench in favor of players with more favorable daily efficiency metrics. We are proceeding with caution regarding **JJ Bleday**, whose 52.54 score is bolstered by weather but hampered by a -14% platoon disadvantage against Houser, requiring us to monitor his real-time output closely. With **Will Smith** confirmed on the IL, our roster depth remains intact, but we are keeping a close watch on any late-inning tactical shifts that might demand a substitution for **Justin Crawford** or **Daulton Varsho** if those specific matchups tighten as the game progresses.",
